## Input contract (production-equivalent)

Each stage was driven with the exact env + prompt CP would emit. See
`<stage>/inputs.json` for the literal values. Surfaces that matter for the
SDK launcher (`packages/core/runtimes/claude-agent/launch.ts`):

- `ARK_SESSION_ID`, `ARK_SESSION_DIR`, `ARK_WORKTREE`, `ARK_PROMPT_FILE`
- `ARK_STAGE`, `ARK_MAX_TURNS`, `ARK_MODEL`
- `ARK_COMPAT=bedrock` (enables the in-process bedrock-compat proxy)
- `ARK_SYSTEM_PROMPT_APPEND` (the agent YAML's rendered system_prompt)
- `ARK_TENANT_ID`
- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`, `ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS`
- File at `$ARK_PROMPT_FILE` holds the task prompt (rendered)

## What this proves

- ✓ The per-session pod can complete a docs-flow E2E given correct inputs.
- ✓ The claude-agent SDK + bedrock-compat proxy + harinder JWT + haiku slug path works.
- ✓ Authed git clone + push against private Bitbucket works.
- ✓ Bitbucket REST API PR-create works with our SSM credentials.

Implication: any failure in production E2E with the same image + DB +
secrets is in the **orchestration layer** (Temporal workflow, CP dispatch
pipeline, arkd integration), not the pod itself.

